.claude

# graphify writes its knowledge graph here. Never commit it: graphify
# has no secret-redaction pass, and docstrings plus NOTE/TODO/FIXME
# comments are copied verbatim into graph.json node labels and inlined
# into graph.html. A key sitting in a comment anywhere under api/ or
# supabase-migrations/ would land in these files in cleartext.
#
# It also closes a real attack path: graphify's own skill files run
# `$(cat graphify-out/.graphify_python)` unquoted in command position,
# so a committed graphify-out/ is an execution vector for anyone who
# checks the repo out.
graphify-out/

# Agent skills are installed with `npx skills add`, which drops the
# skill's own files here. That payload is third-party and reinstallable,
# so it's ignored the way node_modules is — but skills-lock.json IS
# committed, since it pins the source and content hash and is what makes
# the install reproducible.
.agents

